### Program Overview

The provided source code is a unit test suite for a class named `IECore.BasicPreset`. This class is designed to handle the creation, application, and saving/loading of presets for objects that implement the `IECore.Parameterised` interface. The tests cover various scenarios such as copying parameters, loading and saving presets, handling different types of parameters like Bool, Float, Class, and CompoundVector, and ensuring that the presets correctly apply changes to the target objects.

### Classes and Their Purposes

#### `TestBasicPreset`

This class inherits from `unittest.TestCase`, which is a standard testing framework in Python. It contains several test methods to validate the functionality of the `IECore.BasicPreset` class.

### Fields and Member Variables

No fields or member variables are explicitly defined within the `TestBasicPreset` class itself. Instead, it uses instances of `IECore.Parameterised`, `IECore.BoolParameter`, `IECore.FloatParameter`, `IECore.ClassParameter`, and `IECore.CompoundVectorParameter` to create test cases.

### Functions and Methods

#### `testCopy`

This method tests the ability of `IECore.BasicPreset` to copy parameters from one object to another. It creates two `IECore.Parameter
*************
