for i in range(1, M + 1):
    if M % 2 == 1:
        first_element = start_first_element + (i - 1)
        second_element = start_second_element - (i - 1)
    else:
        first_element = start_first_element + (i - 1)
        second_element = start_second_element - (i - 1)
    
    print(f"({first_element}, {second_element})")
```

This code reads two integers `N` and `M` from the user, determines the ranges for the first and second elements of the pairs based on whether `M` is odd or even, and then prints the pairs accordingly.
