## Classes and Their Purposes

### CatmullRomCurve Class
The `CatmullRomCurve` class is designed to represent a spline curve using Catmull-Rom interpolation. It allows adding points with associated properties such as size, color, transparency, and UV coordinates. The class provides methods to evaluate the curve at any given parameter value, as well as to perform adaptive tessellation to ensure smooth curves.

#### Fields
- **points**: A vector of `Point` objects representing the control points of the curve.
- **sizes**: A vector of `float` values representing the sizes of the control points.
- **cols**: A vector of `Spectrum` objects representing the colors of the control points.
